    summary: "This unit reviews the whole course and prepares learners for the final examination, which covers both halves: the idea of covenant, Noah, Abraham, Moses, David and the new covenant in Christ.",
    scripture: ["Hebrews 8:6-13", "Genesis 15:1-6"], more: ["Genesis 9:8-17", "Exodus 24:1-8", "2 Samuel 7:12-16"], memory: "2 Corinthians 1:20",
    minutes: 60,
    objectives: ["Summarise the main teaching of the course from Noah to the new covenant", "Link each covenant to its sign, promise and Scripture", "Prepare for the final examination and commit to live in covenant faithfulness"],
    terms: [["Covenant", "God's binding promise to his people, with a sign."], ["Mediator", "One who stands between God and people, supremely Christ."], ["New covenant", "God's covenant of forgiveness, a new heart and the Spirit, sealed in Christ's blood."]],
    intro: "We have followed the great thread of Scripture, the covenants of God. We have seen God preserve the earth with Noah, call and justify Abraham by faith, redeem Israel and give them his law at Sinai, promise David an eternal king and announce a new covenant that Christ established in his blood. Today we gather the threads and prepare for the final examination. May we hold fast to the promises of God and walk in his faithfulness.",
    context: "This is the default week for the final examination, which covers learning from both halves of the course. Churches may hold the examination during class or on another date, using this session for review. Hebrews 8 and 2 Corinthians 1:20 sum up the course: the promises of God find their Yes in Christ, who mediates a better covenant.",
    observe: "The covenants together tell a single story. The promise to Adam's race is carried by the covenant with Noah, narrowed through Abraham, expressed in law at Sinai, centred on a king in David and fulfilled in Christ's new covenant. Each has its sign: rainbow, circumcision, Sabbath, throne, and bread and cup. Throughout, God's faithfulness is constant and the response he asks is faith and obedience.",
    points: [
      ["God's covenants reveal his faithful love and plan", "We reviewed the meaning of covenant, the covenant with Noah and the rainbow, the call and justification of Abraham, circumcision and Moriah. Recall Genesis 9, 12, 15 and 17, Deuteronomy 7:9 and Hebrews 6:13-18. God binds himself in love and keeps his word."],
      ["The covenants unfold toward Christ", "At Sinai, God redeemed and gave the law, the tabernacle and sacrifices. The prophets called for faithfulness. God promised David an everlasting king and announced a new covenant. Recall Exodus 19 and 24, Deuteronomy 30, 2 Samuel 7, Jeremiah 31 and Ezekiel 36. All point to Jesus."],
      ["Christ established the new covenant, and we live in its promises", "Jesus sealed the new covenant in his blood, and we receive forgiveness, a new heart and the Spirit by faith. Baptism and the Lord's Supper are its signs. We live in faith, obedience and mission. Recall Luke 22:20, Hebrews 8 and 9, Romans 11 and Ephesians 2."],
    ],
    discuss: [
      ["What are the three most important things you have learned in this course?", "Let learners share and connect each one to a passage of Scripture from the course, then summarise on the board."],
      ["How has this course changed the way you read the Old Testament?", "Invite honest testimonies from learners and give thanks to God together for what has been learned."],
      ["Which part of the course do you want to study more?", "Note ideas for further study and point learners to the next courses in the library, so interest turns into continued learning."],
      ["How can we help others see how the whole Bible points to Christ?", "Conversation, teaching and story. Encourage learners to name one person and one practical way to share the message."],
    ],
    apply: "Prepare for the final examination by reviewing the revision map and memory verses. Write a personal statement of what you believe about God's covenant faithfulness and how you will live it. Share it with a friend.",
    activity: "Run a relay: teams race to match each covenant to its sign, promise and key passage, and add one-sentence applications. Finish by reading 2 Corinthians 1:20 together as an act of thanksgiving.",
    takeHome: "Review your notes and the revision map. Write five practice questions with answers and test someone.",
    prayer: "Thank God for his faithful covenants. Ask for calm minds for the examination. Pray that what we have learned will deepen our trust in Christ.",
    teacher: "Explain the final examination arrangements clearly: time, number of questions and how results are released. Encourage anxious learners. If the exam is on another date, use the session for review. Mention that next week is revision and commissioning.",
    assess: "This unit is the final examination week. The final examination covers Lessons 1 to 12 and 14 to 24 and is built from the approved question bank following the curriculum blueprint.",
    mcq1: ["Which covenant sign is connected with Noah?", ["The rainbow", "Circumcision", "The Sabbath", "The bread and cup"], 0, "The rainbow is the sign of the covenant with Noah."],
